# NeoBench program entry.
#
# The first line of a file that is neither blank nor a comment may say
# what the file is for.  "program = name" makes the file an entry rather
# than a document: choosing it in Files starts that program instead of
# opening it, so a drawer can hold a program the way the start menu
# does.  The name is one of the desktop's own -- files, clock, monitor,
# about, preferences, neotext, vlc, neoshell -- and a file that names
# anything else, or that says nothing at all, opens in the reader as it
# always has.
#
# NeoShell is the command line: the NeoCommands, read against the file
# store the ROM carries and against what the hardware probe found, and
# nothing outside either.  It is also what boots in place of the
# desktop when Escape is pressed during the hold, and what Config/
# boot.cfg's "failsafe = on" asks for, so this entry is the third way
# to it -- the one that keeps the desktop standing underneath while you
# are at the prompt.  "desktop" closes it again from the inside, which
# is the same command the boot-time shell uses to let the compositor up.

program = neoshell
